---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { findHeroImage } from "../../lib/hero-images";

const lessons = (await getCollection("lessons"))
  .filter((l) => l.data.listed !== false)
  .toSorted((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<PageLayout
  title="Lessons"
  description="LLMs Unplugged lessons: complete workshop sessions with timings, prep notes and materials lists."
>
  <h1>Lessons</h1>

  <p>
    A lesson is a complete session: a sequence of <a href="/modules/">modules</a> with timings, prep
    notes, and a materials list. Pick the one that fits your group.
  </p>

  <div class="at-card-grid at-card-grid--2">
    {lessons.map((lesson) => <Card
      href={`/lessons/${lesson.id}/`}
      title={lesson.data.title}
      headingLevel="h2"
      image={lesson.data.heroImage ? findHeroImage(`hero-${lesson.data.heroImage}`) : undefined}
    >
      <p class="card-description">{lesson.data.description}</p>
      <p class="card-badges">
        {lesson.data.audience} &middot; {lesson.data.duration} &middot;{" "}
        {lesson.data.flavour}
      </p>
    </Card>)}
  </div>

  <p>
    Not sure where to start? Each card above gives the audience and length, so pick the one that
    fits your room. If you'd rather assemble your own session from the parts, browse the
    <a href="/modules/">modules</a>. Giving a talk rather than running a workshop? The
    <a href="/talks/">talks</a> hand the whole audience a model on search sheets and run it from the
    stage.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
